+# Local CocoaPods dependency
+
+- Upstream: https://github.com/WhisperSystems/libsignal-protocol-c.git
+- Baseline: `4a137eaf4eb4421949e2e1dde9f11ec7bc07b88f` (`v2.3.2`).
+- Local branch: `codex/ios-local-dependencies`.
+- The upstream revision does not contain a root CocoaPods spec. `SignalProtocolC.podspec.json` was copied from the installed CocoaPods trunk spec for 2.3.2.
+- Original spec checksum from the application's Podfile.lock: `051512e9f3abfeb4120c5e9673af9ae0ee370070`.
+- Original spec SHA-256: `e59ec2d23a59490dc703122b7b2d053262bc57ac2f745e7e7894677c72a6dfd4`.
+- Setup change: header search paths use `$(PODS_TARGET_SRCROOT)/src` instead of `$(PODS_ROOT)/SignalProtocolC/src`, preserving all four search directories. This supports a development pod outside Pods/.
+- No cryptographic source, wire format, or library version changes.
+
+Point `SignalProtocolC` at this directory with CocoaPods `:path`.
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index f1c5474..adde2e7 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -71,6 +71,77 @@ CMake toolchain files have been included from the following sources:
 * [iOS](https://code.google.com/archive/p/ios-cmake)
 * [BlackBerry 10](https://github.com/blackberry/OGRE/blob/master/src/CMake/toolchain/blackberry.toolchain.cmake)
 
+# Explicit OMEMO2 profile (Xabber fork)
+
+The `omemo_keys.h`, `omemo_wire.h` and `omemo_session.h` APIs implement the
+cryptographic dependency profile of [XEP-0384 0.9.1](https://xmpp.org/extensions/xep-0384.html),
+`urn:xmpp:omemo:2`. Call these APIs explicitly. Existing Signal APIs and their
+session records retain their legacy format.
+
+- Identity keys on the wire are raw Ed25519 (32 bytes); other public keys are
+  raw X25519 (32 bytes). Imported scalars follow RFC7748 decoding. XEdDSA signs
+  with the corresponding identity; verification accepts RFC8032 signatures.
+- A signed prekey and a mandatory one-time prekey initialize X3DH; both IDs
+  are in `1..2^31-1`. X3DH, root and message HKDF use the OMEMO info strings.
+- The bounded protobuf codec follows `protobuf/OMEMO.proto`, including unknown
+  fields, and preserves the original inner bytes for AD + message MAC16.
+  No legacy Signal version byte or MAC8 is inserted.
+- Double Ratchet advances within repeated KEX packets with the same EK. An
+  authenticated reply confirms the session. Failed operations leave state
+  unchanged. Skipped keys use the XEP limit of 1000 with FIFO eviction and a
+  local retention policy of 1000 subsequent accepted receive events. Sends,
+  failures and replay candidates do not age keys. The receive event that
+  creates a skipped key gives it age zero; its 1000th later receive erases it.
+- `encrypt` accepts exactly a wrapped content key + MAC (48 bytes), or a
+  32-byte all-zero empty control message. This API does not encrypt the outer
+  stanza payload or implement PEP, trust, SCE or application ACK routing.
+
+A C session is not internally synchronized; its provider context must outlive
+it. Serialize access and **atomically persist the new secret snapshot before
+releasing ciphertext or accepting plaintext**. For the first received KEX,
+persist the authenticated session and consume its OPK in the same transaction.
+Repeated KEX must look up the existing session by its authenticated peer/EK;
+passing every packet to `begin_bob` would recreate state. Snapshots have their
+own profile magic/version and must never be parsed as legacy Signal records.
+The caller supplies protected storage and rollback protection for snapshots.
+Local snapshots now serialize as version 2 with receive-event ages. Version 1
+imports preserve every key, ratchet counter, EK and pending state, giving
+retained keys a full new retention window. The local event epoch is rebased at
+`UINT64_MAX` without changing key ages. Rejection of application payload/SCE
+must discard its candidate snapshot, including event ages and key erasure.
+`SG_ERR_DUPLICATE_MESSAGE` reports a stale-counter candidate: once its MK has
+been consumed or erased, the C session cannot authenticate that ciphertext.
+Callers must prove an exact previously accepted packet before treating it as
+an authenticated duplicate.
+
+Parser/signature input caps of 1 MiB are local resource limits, not XEP limits.
+Ed25519 verification additionally requires canonical encodings/scalars and
+nonzero prime-subgroup identity and R points.
+
+## Profile tests
+
+These standalone suites use `assert`, the existing crypto provider and CMake;
+Check is only needed for the original Signal test suite. Assertions remain
+enabled even with a Release configuration.
+
+```sh
+cmake -S . -B build-omemo -DBUILD_TESTING=OFF -DBUILD_OMEMO_TESTING=ON \
+  -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug -DCMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.5
+cmake --build build-omemo
+(cd build-omemo && ctest --output-on-failure)
+python3 tests/omemo/reference_vector.py
+```
+
+Tests include published RFC8032/RFC7748 vectors, independent X3DH/ratchet/
+AES/protobuf/MAC bytes, repeated KEX and persistence, skipped messages/replay,
+authentication and crypto-provider failure rollback. The Objective-C wrapper
+and iOS integration add XCTest and independent CryptoKit verification.
+
+Whole-library UBSan reports existing signed-shift issues in the inherited
+Donna/Ed25519 implementation. Passing profile assertions or ASan does not mean
+that the entire upstream arithmetic implementation is UBSan-clean. Live
+cross-client interoperability remains a separate verification requirement.
+
